just like this gun.

171
00:28:16,669 --> 00:28:20,594
And in the most recent period
of this 600-year history,

172
00:28:20,618 --> 00:28:24,470
many great firearms designers appeared
and created famous handguns.

173
00:28:24,471 --> 00:28:25,471
Samuel Colt.

174
00:28:28,300 --> 00:28:32,193
The Single Action Army he created
became a best-seller

175
00:28:32,217 --> 00:28:36,312
during the expansion of the American West
and helped establish Colt's reputation.

176
00:28:36,313 --> 00:28:40,330
Colt's first semi-automatic pistol,
the Model 1900.

177
00:28:48,930 --> 00:28:53,116
M1911, which was later
improved, has been an official

178
00:28:53,140 --> 00:28:56,942
U.S. service pistol for roughly 75 years,
from 1911 until the mid-1980s.

179
00:28:58,429 --> 00:29:01,206
It is still produced in forms commonly
known as the Government Model

180
00:29:01,230 --> 00:29:04,202
after establishing the foundation
for large-caliber semi-automatic pistols.

181
00:29:14,259 --> 00:29:21,710
Horace Smith and Daniel B. Wesson.

182
00:29:21,710 --> 00:29:26,670
Together they founded Smith & Wesson.

183
00:29:28,494 --> 00:29:31,391
The Military & Police revolver
became a highly refined

184
00:29:31,415 --> 00:29:34,392
