187
00:29:51,799 --> 00:29:59,550
Peter Paul Mauser.

188
00:30:01,259 --> 00:30:04,925
The Mauser military pistol,
known for its distinctive design,

189
00:30:04,949 --> 00:30:09,022
was one of the world's first
mass-produced military semi-automatic pistols.

190
00:30:16,319 --> 00:30:20,129
Georg Luger. The distinctive
toggle-lock action

191
00:30:20,153 --> 00:30:24,132
is the trademark feature
of the Luger pistol.

192
00:30:24,919 --> 00:30:27,822
The famous P08 was adopted
by the German military

193
00:30:27,846 --> 00:30:30,762
and served through both
World Wars.

194
00:31:03,610 --> 00:31:11,610
John M. Browning.

195
00:31:11,611 --> 00:31:15,272
He designed pistols such as the Model 1900,
as well as rifles and machine guns,

196
00:31:15,296 --> 00:31:19,032
and became known as one of the great
geniuses of firearms design.

197
00:31:20,419 --> 00:31:23,166
His consistent and advanced
design philosophy

198
00:31:23,190 --> 00:31:26,072
had an enormous influence
on modern semi-automatic pistols.

199
00:31:26,073 --> 00:31:31,110
The Browning Hi-Power
was another of his landmark designs.

200
00:31:46,380 --> 00:31:54,380
Walther.

201
00:31:56,369 --> 00:32:02,870
Among Walther's many fine designs,
the P38 has one of the most distinctive forms.

202
00:32:03,219 --> 00:32:09,050
It was one of the first military pistols
to use a practical double-action trigger.

203
00:32:09,051 --> 00:32:13,300
As the P1, the design continued
in service with the German military.

204
